{
  "_comment": "Generated by hardware/kicad/recorder/generate_pcb.py; the routing and open_items blocks are refreshed by route_pcb.py. Footprint XY for the recorder PCB; keep this file in sync with recorder.kicad_pcb. Origin is the magnet-ring (Pixelsnap) centre; +X phone right, +Y toward the camera bar. The board and lid were spun 180\u00b0 around that origin so J2 sits at the phone-top end; the tray clocking magnet stays at 6 o'clock. Edit both files when a part moves.",
  "board": {
    "width_mm": 59.6,
    "height_mm": 85.6,
    "thickness_mm": 0.8,
    "layers": [
      "F.Cu",
      "In1.Cu (GND)",
      "In2.Cu (VDD33)",
      "B.Cu"
    ],
    "finish": "ENIG",
    "usb_diff_ohm": null,
    "usb_signalling": "USB 2.0 full speed, 12 Mbps",
    "usb_diff_note": "Not impedance controlled, on purpose. The ESP32-S3 USB-OTG peripheral is full speed only (12 Mbps, no high-speed PHY: Espressif's USB overview table marks ESP32-S3 'USB OTG High-Speed = X'). F.Cu sits 0.1 mm above the In1 GND plane in this stackup, where a 90 ohm differential pair would need roughly 0.06 mm traces, well under the 0.127 mm any quick-turn fab will run. Rather than thicken the prepreg for a requirement the silicon does not have, D+/D- run as a 0.2 mm pair on a 0.4 mm pitch over solid In1 GND, which is near 75 ohm differential by first-order microstrip. The run is long for a USB pair because U1's USB pads are on the module's top row, the far side of a 15.9 mm module from the connector, and its castellations leave 0.05 mm between pads so nothing crosses the footprint. At full-speed edge rates it is still electrically short. Measured copper is in hardware/kicad/recorder/placement.json under routing.usb, written by route_pcb.py from the board itself. Do not re-type those millimetres into this sentence: this note and the one in placement.json each carried their own hand-typed lengths and both went stale at the first reroute.",
    "outline_rect_mm": [
      [
        -29.8,
        -42.8
      ],
      [
        29.8,
        42.8
      ]
    ],
    "b_cu_faces_phone": true
  },
