  "footprint_substitutions": {},
  "open_items": [
    "SW1 is a side-actuated Panasonic EVQP7C01P (JLCPCB C388883). The record button is on the phone-left wall when the accessory is snapped on the phone. Its actuator tip sits 0.6 mm inside the board edge; the TPU pill nub spans that gap. Pin 1 carries BTN and pin 2 carries GND. Check the press feel on the first assembled board: 2.2 N is firmer than the 1.6 N alternatives.",
    "Download is four F.Cu pads (TP_BOOT, TP_EN, TP_GND, TP_3V3) beside the MCU. Hold GPIO0 to GND, pulse EN. No Boot/Reset switches and no UART header.",
    "USB D+/D- are not impedance controlled, on purpose: the ESP32-S3 USB peripheral is full speed only, and 90 ohm on this 0.1 mm prepreg would need traces narrower than any quick-turn fab will run. The pair is 0.2 mm wide on a 0.4 mm pitch over solid In1 GND, near 75 ohm differential by first-order microstrip.",
    "MK1's land pattern is a locally adapted copy in PSV.pretty, not the drawing in the Infineon datasheet. The ring pad and its stencil aperture were moved out to 0.95 mm so copper clears the 0.8 mm sound port by 0.32 mm. Check the acoustic seal on the first assembled board.",
    "Pixel body and Pixelsnap ring numbers in hardware/cad/params.json are published defaults. Caliper a real phone and a real magnet ring before cutting metal.",
    "kicad-cli pcb drc --schematic-parity reports notes on spare ESP32-S3 castellations and NC pins, four mounting holes, and three footprint fields the sheet leaves blank (BT1's description, J2's datasheet, J3's description). Copper DRC is clean.",
    "J2 is Xinyangze YZ103915020T-04025-02 (LCSC C6276862) at (0, 36), rot 0, on the phone-top / camera end. The tray clocking magnet stays at 6 o'clock. Vendor drawing is a 22.30 x 7.70 x 2.00 mm stadium. Cable male is YZP0048-20048-04025-03 / C5126845. Pin 1 VBUS, 2 USB_DM, 3 USB_DP, 4 GND until a click-test says otherwise. No Type-C Rd.",
    "The Jauch LP305166JH-PCM-2-WIRES-70MM pack (66 x 51.5 x 3.3 mm, 1200 mAh min) is taped to B.Cu at (0, 0) and wrapped in kapton. About 0.15 mm of air under the wrapped cell so the pouch is not a spacer. BT1 is B.Cu at (-17, 35), west of J2 and just north of the cell, pad 1 VBAT on the west land. Four 5.0 mm posts carry the board.",
    "J3 is CS CSNP32GCR01-AOW (LCSC C2841139) 32 Gbit / 4 GB SD NAND, LGA-8 8.0 x 6.2 mm at (-22, -18). Pin order is 1 DAT2, 2 DAT3, 3 CLK, 4 VSS, 5 CMD, 6 DAT0, 7 DAT1, 8 VDD. Firmware formats FAT on first mount if the chip is blank."
  ],
